=20
+   :term:`KCONFIG_MODE`
+      When used with the :ref:`kernel-yocto <ref-classes-kernel-yocto>`
+      class, specifies the kernel configuration values to use for option=
s not
+      specified in the provided ``defconfig`` file. Valid options are::
+
+         KCONFIG_MODE =3D "alldefconfig"
+         KCONFIG_MODE =3D "allnoconfig"
+
+      In ``alldefconfig`` mode the options not explicitely specified wil=
l be
+      assigned their default value. This is the default handling when us=
ing
+      "in-tree" ``defconfig`` files. A ``defconfig`` file like this can =
be
+      generated using the
+      :ref:`ref-tasks-savedefconfig`
+      task. In ``allnoconfig`` mode the options not explicitely specifie=
d will
+      be disabled in the kernel config. This is the default when using a
+      ``defconfig`` file provided through a meta-layer.
+
